\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Which transports specify a finer field?}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Multiplying the fine transports along a subdivided coarse edge gives one coarse transport. The oriented fine plaquette products inside a coarse cell multiply to its oriented boundary product, as internal edges cancel. Which choices of fine links can realize both prescribed coarse transports and equal shares of the coarse angle? The [scalar plaquette angle](fdip-015V) and the cellular boundary in \ref{fdip-00OW} specify these two constraints.}
